    "question": {
      ":question/id": "015a3f62-2ed2-5053-8533-896aab9a60ae",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=3 x^{2} + x y^{2}$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf{i}+3 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x^{2} + x y^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(6 x + y^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+2 x y\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=\\ln{\\left(t \\right)}$ and $y=3 e^{2 t}$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(6(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})+(3 e^{2 t})^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+2(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(3 e^{2 t})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(9 e^{4 t} + 6 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+6 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 e^{2 t})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+6 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =((9 e^{4 t} + 6 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+6 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+6 e^{2 t}\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =((9 e^{4 t} + 6 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}))\\left(\\frac{1}{t}\\right)+(6 e^{2 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)})(6 e^{2 t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{6 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}+\\frac{9 e^{4 t}}{t}+36 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} \\\\  & =36 e^{4 t} \\ln{\\left(t \\right)} + \\frac{9 e^{4 t}}{t} + \\frac{6 \\ln{\\left(t \\right)}}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
